      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/a9a28c/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-09-20T23:00:34.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So this is one of those questions about the meaning of \"turn\". The text on Annubis states, \"The first time a non-environment card is destroyed each turn, this card deals the non-environment target with the second highest hp 2 infernal damage.\" Does \"turn\" mean environment turn, villain turn, and hero turn? Or does it mean the overall turn--i.e., the \"tunr\" that starts with the villain and ends with the environment?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:13.296Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
